<%# The row a reply streams into, replaced by threads/_message the moment the
    reply is complete.

    Keyed on the question it answers, not on the conversation. A student who
    asks again before the contact has replied would otherwise put a second
    element with the same id on the page: getElementById returns the first, so
    both replies streamed into one paragraph and the other row was stranded
    there for the rest of the visit. %>
<%= render layout: "shared/transcript_row", locals: {
      id: dom_id(question, :pending),
      speaker: contact.full_name,
      from_contact: true,
      body: nil,
      body_id: dom_id(question, :pending_body),
      meta: tag.span(t("threads.replying"), class: "kick text-xs text-accent")
    } do %><% end %>
